   "text": {
    "L1": "A length is the number of one-centimetre spaces from one end to the other.",
    "L2": "So place the start at zero, then read the mark at the other end.",
    "L3": "If the start is not zero, subtract the start reading from the end reading.",
    "L4": "For a stick from 2 to 11, the length is 11 minus 2, or 9 centimetres.",
    "L5": "One metre equals 100 centimetres, so 2 metres equals 200 centimetres.",
    "L6": "Do not join the digits: 1 metre 5 centimetres is 105 centimetres.",
    "L7": "Use centimetres for small things and metres for big things such as rooms and pitches.",
    "L8": "Now a crayon goes from 3 to 9. Tap its length."
   },
